WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:09.958
In this lesson, you will look after your account: your password, your calendar, your privacy choices, and two-step sign-in.

2
00:00:10.813 --> 00:00:14.629
Click Settings at the bottom of the left menu.

3
00:00:15.486 --> 00:00:25.494
To change your password, enter your current password, and a new one of at least eight characters. Then click Update password.

4
00:00:26.357 --> 00:00:39.509
Click Show my calendar link to get a private address. Paste it into Google, Apple or Outlook calendar, and your deadlines appear there. Keep the link private.

5
00:00:40.369 --> 00:00:57.049
You can add your birthday, without a year, so your team can celebrate with you. And if your company has turned on WhatsApp, enter your number and tick the box to receive alerts. We never send a message without your tick.

6
00:00:57.923 --> 00:01:11.291
Under Your data and privacy, you can download everything we hold about you, ask for a correction, or ask for deletion. This is your right under India's data protection law.

7
00:01:12.154 --> 00:01:23.482
Now the most important security step, especially for founders, who can open bank details. Click Security, then two-step sign-in.

8
00:01:24.347 --> 00:01:30.107
Click Set up two-step sign-in. You will see a QR code.

9
00:01:30.965 --> 00:01:47.165
On your phone, open Google Authenticator or Microsoft Authenticator, and choose Scan a QR code. Point it at this screen. If you cannot scan, type the long key shown underneath into the app instead.

10
00:01:48.039 --> 00:02:06.015
The app now shows a six digit code. Type it here, and click Turn on. You will then be shown eight recovery codes. Save them somewhere safe. Each one works once, if you ever lose your phone.

11
00:02:06.875 --> 00:02:20.339
From then on, signing in asks for your password, and a code from your phone. If you are locked out with no phone and no recovery codes, another founder can switch it off for you.

12
00:02:21.205 --> 00:02:30.757
That completes the lessons for employees and interns. The next two lessons are for managers, founders and group owners.
